    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# API Integration Pipeline\n\n**Owned By:** Anubhav Kumar Srivastava\n**Last Updated:** 27-Sept-2026\n\nFetches orders from the Academy API, enriches them with customer data, routes orders by priority and region, and sends eligible enterprise orders to a priority queue in batches.\n\n## Flow\n\n1. **GetOrders:** Fetches paginated orders from the Academy API.\n2. **GetCustomers:** Fetches customer records in parallel with orders.\n3. **MergeOrdersCustomers:** Joins orders and customers using `customer_id`.\n4. **AggregateOrders + SendToOrdersQueue:** Aggregates and sends enriched orders to the order queue.\n5. **CheckSubscriptionTier:** Splits enterprise customers from other customers.\n6. **FilterDelivered + BatchPriorityOrders:** Filters undelivered enterprise orders and processes them in batches.\n7. **SendToPriorityQueue:** Sends enterprise orders to the priority processing queue.\n8. **RouteByRegion:** Routes non-enterprise orders by region — North, South, East, West, or fallback.\n9. **FinalizePipeline:** Sends the final pipeline summary for assessment.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n* Requires: **n8n Academy API Key** credential\n* Requires: **X-Assessment-ID** header for Academy API requests\n\n## Error Handling\n\n* HTTP requests can retry automatically for transient API failures.\n* Customer API failures can be handled using fallback customer data.\n* Regional fallback handles orders with unknown or unsupported regions.\n\n**Part of:** n8n Foundations Program — Course N8N102, Section 1\n\nGood documentation makes the workflow easier to understand, troubleshoot, maintain, and hand over to another developer.\n",
        "height": 752,
        "width": 912
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -960,
        -304
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "e756c02f-a508-4f57-9bd0-be544d1325c5",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    }
